    "body": "Sorry if this was already suggested and/or discussed, or maybe I'm late to the party :grin: . But someone in another thread mentioned that malicious website owners could show a fake prompt to get users to click/gesture, which would defeat the purpose of placing it behind a user gesture. Would it make sense to limit the notification permission request to users who have installed the website as a PWA? At that point, I'd think a user would expect the app to behave like a native one on a mobile device and be able to send push notifications.",
